# CI Pipeline

## Structure

CI runs on **pull requests**, not on the publish jobs.

- `pr-ci.yml` — triggers on PRs targeting `main` or `master`, runs lint → type check → test
- `deploy.yml` — triggers on push to `main`, builds and pushes ARM64 images (no CI steps)
- `build-pi.yml` — triggers on push to `master`, builds and pushes ARM64 images (no CI steps)

Both `main` and `master` are **protected branches**. Branch protection requires the `ci` check from `pr-ci.yml` to pass before a PR can be merged. This is the gate — it does not live in the publish workflows.

## CI job (pr-ci.yml)

```yaml
- name: Lint (ruff)
  run: ruff check .

- name: Type check (mypy)
  run: mypy app/

- name: Test (pytest)
  run: pytest
```

All three steps must pass. Do not remove or skip any of them.

## What not to do

- Do **not** add CI steps to `deploy.yml` or `build-pi.yml` — they run after a protected merge, so CI has already passed.
- Do **not** bypass branch protection or merge without a passing `ci` check.
- Do **not** add a new publish workflow without ensuring the target branch is protected.
